{"id": "ccp8", "code": "CCP8", "label": "Sauvegardes & restaurations", "questions": [{"n": 1, "title": "Types sauvegardes", "section": null, "html": "<p>Quelle sauvegarde copie uniquement fichiers modifiés depuis dernière complète ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "Complète"}, {"l": "B", "html": "Différentielle"}, {"l": "C", "html": "Incrémentale"}, {"l": "D", "html": "Synthétique"}], "answer": ["B"]}, {"n": 2, "title": "Restauration rapide", "section": null, "html": "<p>Quel type nécessite MOINS de bandes pour restaurer ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "Complète + Incrémentales  (si dernière incrémentale récente)"}, {"l": "B", "html": "Complète + Différentielle"}, {"l": "C", "html": "Incrémentale seule"}, {"l": "D", "html": "Différentielle seule"}], "answer": ["B"]}, {"n": 3, "title": "Règle 3-2-1", "section": null, "html": "<p>Que signifie règle sauvegarde 3-2-1 ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "3 copies, 2 supports différents, 1 hors site"}, {"l": "B", "html": "3 serveurs, 2 datacenters, 1 cloud"}, {"l": "C", "html": "3 jours, 2 semaines, 1 mois"}, {"l": "D", "html": "3 bandes, 2 disques, 1 cloud"}], "answer": ["A"]}, {"n": 4, "title": "RPO (Recovery Point Objective)", "section": null, "html": "<p>RPO = 4h signifie ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "Restauration en 4h max"}, {"l": "B", "html": "Perte données acceptable = 4h max"}, {"l": "C", "html": "Sauvegarde toutes les 4h"}, {"l": "D", "html": "Rétention 4h"}], "answer": ["B"]}, {"n": 5, "title": "Veeam Backup", "section": null, "html": "<p>Quelle technologie Veeam utilise pour sauvegardes incrémentielles rapides ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "Snapshots"}, {"l": "B", "html": "Changed Block Tracking (CBT)"}, {"l": "C", "html": "Deduplication"}, {"l": "D", "html": "Compression"}], "answer": ["B"]}, {"n": 6, "title": "Snapshot vs Backup", "section": null, "html": "<p>Différence principale snapshot/sauvegarde ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "Snapshot = instantané même stockage, Backup = copie séparée"}, {"l": "B", "html": "Aucune différence"}, {"l": "C", "html": "Snapshot permanent, Backup temporaire"}, {"l": "D", "html": "Snapshot lent, Backup rapide"}], "answer": ["A"]}, {"n": 7, "title": "Tar Linux", "section": null, "html": "<p>Commande créer archive compressée ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "<code>tar -xzf backup.tar.gz /data</code>"}, {"l": "B", "html": "<code>tar -czf backup.tar.gz /data</code>"}, {"l": "C", "html": "<code>tar -tzf backup.tar.gz /data</code>"}, {"l": "D", "html": "<code>tar -rzf backup.tar.gz /data</code>"}], "answer": ["B"]}, {"n": 8, "title": "Windows Server Backup", "section": null, "html": "<p>Commande PowerShell sauvegarde complète vers E: ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "<code>Start-Backup -Target E:</code>"}, {"l": "B", "html": "<code>wbadmin start backup -backupTarget:E: -include:C: -allCritical</code>"}, {"l": "C", "html": "<code>Backup-Volume C: -Destination E:</code>"}, {"l": "D", "html": "<code>New-Backup -Path E: -Source C:</code>"}], "answer": ["B"]}, {"n": 9, "title": "Baie NAS", "section": null, "html": "<p>Avantage principal NAS pour sauvegardes ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "Performance maximale"}, {"l": "B", "html": "Stockage réseau centralisé accessible"}, {"l": "C", "html": "Chiffrement matériel"}, {"l": "D", "html": "Coût faible"}], "answer": ["B"]}, {"n": 10, "title": "Bande LTO", "section": null, "html": "<p>LTO-7 capacité native ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "1.5 TB"}, {"l": "B", "html": "3 TB"}, {"l": "C", "html": "6 TB"}, {"l": "D", "html": "12 TB"}], "answer": ["C"]}, {"n": 11, "title": "Rsync Linux", "section": null, "html": "<p>Que fait <code>rsync -av /source/ /backup/</code> ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "Copie complète écrasant destination"}, {"l": "B", "html": "Synchronisation incrémentale préservant attributs"}, {"l": "C", "html": "Compression archives"}, {"l": "D", "html": "Suppression fichiers source"}], "answer": ["B"]}, {"n": 12, "title": "Deduplication", "section": null, "html": "<p>Quel gain typique déduplication sauvegardes ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "10-20%"}, {"l": "B", "html": "30-50%"}, {"l": "C", "html": "80-90%"}, {"l": "D", "html": "5%"}], "answer": ["B"]}, {"n": 13, "title": "Veeam réplication", "section": null, "html": "<p>Différence Backup / Replication Veeam ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "Backup = fichiers, Replication = VMs complètes"}, {"l": "B", "html": "Backup = archive, Replication = VM prête démarrage"}, {"l": "C", "html": "Aucune"}, {"l": "D", "html": "Backup quotidien, Replication temps réel"}], "answer": ["B"]}, {"n": 14, "title": "Restauration granulaire", "section": null, "html": "<p>Que permet restauration granulaire Exchange ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "Restaurer base complète uniquement"}, {"l": "B", "html": "Restaurer emails individuels depuis backup"}, {"l": "C", "html": "Restaurer serveur complet"}, {"l": "D", "html": "Restaurer config uniquement"}], "answer": ["B"]}, {"n": 15, "title": "GFS (Grandfather-Father-Son)", "section": null, "html": "<p>Schéma GFS typique ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "Quotidien-Hebdomadaire-Mensuel"}, {"l": "B", "html": "Complet-Différentiel-Incrémental"}, {"l": "C", "html": "Local-Distant-Cloud"}, {"l": "D", "html": "Primaire-Secondaire-Tertiaire"}], "answer": ["A"]}, {"n": 16, "title": "Test restauration", "section": null, "html": "<p>Fréquence recommandée tests restauration ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "Annuelle"}, {"l": "B", "html": "Trimestrielle"}, {"l": "C", "html": "Après chaque sauvegarde"}, {"l": "D", "html": "Jamais (automatique)"}], "answer": ["B"]}, {"n": 17, "title": "Chiffrement sauvegardes", "section": null, "html": "<p>Algorithme recommandé chiffrement ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "DES"}, {"l": "B", "html": "MD5"}, {"l": "C", "html": "AES-256"}, {"l": "D", "html": "Base64"}], "answer": ["C"]}, {"n": 18, "title": "Commande dd Linux", "section": null, "html": "<p